# Next.js Core

Expert-level Next.js + TypeScript practices for this project.

## App Router

- Use server components by default; add `'use client'` only when necessary
- File-based routing under `src/app/` with `[locale]` segment for i18n
- Use `layout.tsx` for shared layouts, `loading.tsx` for loading states, `error.tsx` for error handling
- `global-error.tsx` at `src/app/global-error.tsx` for root-level failures
- Route handlers for API routes under `src/app/api/`
- Follow Next.js naming conventions for special files

## Async APIs (Next.js 15+)

- `params`, `searchParams`, `cookies()`, and `headers()` are async — await them in server components and route handlers

## TypeScript & code quality

- Use TypeScript for type safety across all source files
- Write clear, readable code; focus on readability over micro-optimization
- Fully implement requested functionality — no TODOs or placeholders
- Reference filenames when discussing changes
- If uncertain, say so instead of guessing

## SEO & metadata

- Implement proper metadata for SEO via `metadata` export or `generateMetadata()`
- Localize metadata per locale (see `i18n-rtl.mdc`)

## Images

- Use `next/image` for optimized images
- Include size data; prefer WebP where appropriate; lazy-load non-critical images

## Environment & configuration

- All secrets and config via environment variables validated in `src/env.ts`
- Never hardcode credentials or bypass `src/env.ts`

## Error handling

- Implement proper error boundaries (`error.tsx`, `global-error.tsx`)
- Use error boundaries for unexpected errors; model expected errors as return values in actions (see `nextjs-data.mdc`)

## Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS for styling (component-level patterns in `nextjs-ui.mdc`)
